{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ve been reviewing why you came in. You’ve been having worsening abdominal pain and vomiting for about two weeks, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been terrible. The pain is way worse than usual—like a 9 out of 10. And I’ve been vomiting up to four liters at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned it feels like one of your partial bowel obstructions. That makes sense. We did a CT scan, and it shows your small bowel is still chronically obstructed, just like before—no new changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not worse? But why does it hurt so much more now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be an 'acute on chronic' flare-up—your usual obstruction, but something’s making it act up. You said you’ve been eating—was that since your last visit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I was told not to, but I was so hungry. I had some soup and crackers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That might be part of the problem. When you have a partial blockage, food can get stuck and make the pain worse. We’re going to keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But how will I get nutrition?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on TPN through your femoral line, which gives you all the nutrients you need. We’ll keep that going and monitor your pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My G-tube hasn’t been draining well either. I think it’s clogged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We saw that. When we flushed it earlier, we found food particles stuck inside. That’s not good. We’ll need to replace it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Again? It just got replaced a few months ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2185-08-11 23:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s frustrating. But if it’s not working, it can’t help decompress your stomach. We’ll schedule the replacement for tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2185-08-12 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2185-08-12 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still bad. I haven’t eaten, like you said, but it’s not helping much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2185-08-12 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you IV Dilaudid for pain and promethazine for nausea. Surgery also looked at your case—they agree it’s not surgical. We’ll keep managing it medically."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2185-08-12 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my femoral line? It’s been leaking a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2185-08-12 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed the cuff is exposed. That increases infection risk. We’ll replace it at the same time as your G-tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2185-08-12 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds like a lot at once."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2185-08-12 09:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. But it’s safer to do both together. The procedure team says it might be tough—there’s a lot of scar tissue from past surgeries."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2185-08-13 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi. Just checking in. Your G-tube fell out overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2185-08-13 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It just slipped out! I didn’t pull it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2185-08-13 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It happens, especially if it’s clogged or not secured well. Don’t worry—we’ll replace it tomorrow with the femoral line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2185-08-13 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been so sad lately. My husband passed two months ago, and his memorial was the day before I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2185-08-13 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m so sorry. That’s a lot to carry. We’ve had psychiatry and social work check in with you. Are you feeling okay emotionally?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2185-08-13 10:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m coping. I just feel overwhelmed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2185-08-13 10:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep supporting you. Your meds are being continued as before—paroxetine, trazodone, and the others."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2185-08-14 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an X-ray this morning. No signs of new obstruction. Your colon has air and contrast, and you’re passing gas. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2185-08-14 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m not blocked worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2185-08-14 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it looks stable. The pain is likely from the chronic obstruction and ileus—your bowel isn’t moving well. But no emergency."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2185-08-15 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with the procedures yesterday. Both the G-tube and femoral line were successfully replaced."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2185-08-15 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt groggy afterward. Was that from the sedation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2185-08-15 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you became very sleepy a few hours after. We were concerned it might be a reaction between your pain meds and sedatives. But your urine tox came back negative, and you’re back to normal now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2185-08-15 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was scared. I couldn’t wake up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2185-08-15 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. It looked serious, but you recovered fully. We’ll be more cautious with sedation in the future."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2185-08-15 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the new G-tube working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2185-08-15 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s draining well. We tested it with contrast and saw good flow into the stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2185-08-15 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the femoral line?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2185-08-15 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s in place, but it was tough to insert. There’s a lot of scar tissue and calcification. If the cuff pulls out again, we might need to use a different vein."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2185-08-15 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. White count dipped a bit but is recovering. Kidney function is good. We’re confident you can go home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2185-08-15 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? I still have some pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2185-08-15 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but it’s manageable with your regular pain meds—morphine PRN. And since you’re not eating, the G-tube can help prevent buildup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2185-08-15 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I promise I won’t eat. I learned my lesson."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2185-08-15 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And keep flushing the G-tube regularly. A home nurse will visit to help with care and check the line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s the day. You’re doing well—pain is better, you’re alert, and your abdomen is soft. We’re discharging you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad, but I’m nervous about managing everything at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have support. The visiting nurse will help with the G-tube and femoral line. And your TPN will continue as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my Lovenox? I’ve been on 40 mg daily for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noted that. It might be higher than needed for prevention. Talk to your hematologist about possibly adjusting the dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my thyroid and dry eyes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking levothyroxine in the morning, two hours before calcium. And use your pilocarpine and Restasis for dry eyes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call if pain worsens, the G-tube stops draining, or you see redness at the line site. Otherwise, follow up with your GI and primary doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And thank you for listening about my husband."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Grief is part of healing too. Take care of yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—what’s that lump near my scar?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We saw a small 2 cm mass on exam. It’s not new—likely scar tissue or a hernia. Mention it at your next visit for monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll bring it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. The discharge papers are ready, and transport is arranged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2185-08-16 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I’m ready to go home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2185-08-11 22:52:00",
    "admission_end": "2185-08-16 15:46:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a complex medical history including sclerosing mesenteritis, chronic small bowel obstruction, and long-term TPN dependence via a femoral line was admitted for worsening abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting. Imaging confirmed stable chronic small bowel obstruction, and her symptoms were attributed to an acute on chronic flare, likely exacerbated by recent oral intake. She was managed non-operatively with NPO status, IV pain control, and eventual transition back to her home pain regimen. During the admission, her G-tube malfunctioned and fell out, requiring replacement, and her femoral line was replaced due to cuff exposure. She experienced transient somnolence post-procedure, likely due to sedative interaction, but returned to baseline. Psychosocial support was provided for grief following her husband's recent death. She was discharged home with visiting nurse services, instructions to remain NPO, and follow-up plans for her vascular access and anticoagulation management.",
    "problems": [
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Other gastrostomy complications",
      "Mechanical complication of other vascular device, implant, and graft",
      "Other alteration of consciousness",
      "Family disruption due to death of family member",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Sicca syndrome",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus"
    ]
  }
}
